help=**Events**\n`!event create | Title | YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm | zone/default | limit/none | description/- | repeat | duration-minutes (optional)`\n`!event list` — upcoming events\n`!event info ID` — details and attendees\n`!event rsvp ID yes|maybe|no` — change RSVP\n`!event cancel ID` — cancel your event\n`!event manage ID` — open host controls on demand\n`!event setup` — guided server setup (admins)\n`!event myzone Europe/Amsterdam` — time shown in private replies\n`!event zones` — time-zone examples\n`!event language` — language support and contribution info\n\n**Example**\n`!event create | Board Game Night | 2026-11-15 19:00 | default | 12 | Bring a game | weekly:4 | 120`\nUse the 24-hour clock. `default` uses the server zone. `1` or `none` means one event; `daily:2`, `weekly:4`, `monthly:3` means a series of 2–12 events. The optional last field is approximate duration in minutes (15–1440); omitted means the server default.\nStart setup in a server or DM me. Events are published only in the selected announcement channel.
zones=**Time-zone examples**\nMoscow — `Europe/Moscow` · Kaliningrad — `Europe/Kaliningrad`\nYekaterinburg — `Asia/Yekaterinburg` · Novosibirsk — `Asia/Novosibirsk`\nVladivostok — `Asia/Vladivostok` · Minsk — `Europe/Minsk`\nAmsterdam — `Europe/Amsterdam` · Berlin — `Europe/Berlin`\nLondon — `Europe/London` · New York — `America/New_York` · Tokyo — `Asia/Tokyo`\n\nAny full IANA zone supported by Node.js is valid. `Europe` alone is not a time zone. Popular city aliases are supported too.
languageSupportInfo=**Language support**\nAvailable languages: {languages}.\n`!event language request` — request a language.\n`!event language submit` — offer or submit a translation file.\nA new `.lang` file can be added without changing bot logic; keys and placeholders must stay intact.
languageSupportUsage=Use `!event language`, `!event language request`, or `!event language submit`.
languageRequestFormReady=Submit a request for a new language here: {url}
languageRequestFormMissing=The language-request form isn't configured yet. The maintainer can set `LANGUAGE_REQUEST_FORM_URL` in `.env` when the form is ready.
languageSubmissionFormReady=Use this form to offer or submit a translation: {url}
languageSubmissionFormMissing=The translation-submission form isn't configured yet. The maintainer can set `LANGUAGE_SUBMISSION_FORM_URL` in `.env` when ready. For now, prepare a `.lang` file based on `lang/en.lang`, translate the values only, preserve keys and `{placeholders}`, then run `npm run check:lang`.
